== Wave 0: Mod List

This wave uses no gameplay-altering mods. The following are approved UI and quality-of-life improvements that do not change game mechanics.

=== Recommended UI / QoL Mods

#mod-panel("Extended Camera Minimod", "https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3339446174", shimazu-vermillion)[
  Extends the maximum zoom-out distance in battle, giving you a better tactical overview of the battlefield. Updated version by Gacsam — fixes crash issues that affected the original 13-year-old mod on modern game builds. No gameplay changes, purely a camera adjustment.
]

=== Bugfixes

#mod-panel("Better Naval Autoresolve", "https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3407913145", shimazu-vermillion)[
  Fixes the notoriously punishing naval autoresolve results, where superior fleets would take disproportionate losses compared to land battles. Does not change any unit stats or game balance — only adjusts the autoresolve calculation to produce fairer outcomes.
]

#mod-panel("Icons Fix", "https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2844242500", shimazu-vermillion)[
  Restores missing building icons (farms for all eras, Nanban trade ports) and fixes icon issues in the Gempei (Rise of the Samurai) campaign. Purely cosmetic — no gameplay changes.
]

#mod-panel("Better Ambush Deployment", "https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1197036915", shimazu-vermillion)[
  Improves the deployment zone placement for ambush battles, giving attackers a more sensible starting position. Compatible with Fall of the Samurai and Rise of the Samurai.
]

#mod-panel("Upstart General Removal", "https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=135017053", shimazu-vermillion)[
  Removes the random "Upstart General" event that could prematurely kill or displace your generals. A pure annoyance fix — no balance or gameplay changes.
]

#mod-panel("Leased Land Demolishable", "https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=487800217", shimazu-vermillion)[
  Allows demolishing the Leased Land building chain, freeing up a slot if you no longer want the leased territory. Pure QoL — no stat or balance changes.
]

=== What NOT to Install

For Wave 0, avoid any mod that:
- Changes unit stats or recruitment
- Alters the campaign map
- Adds new units or buildings
- Modifies AI behavior
- Changes any game balance values

The purpose of Wave 0 is to learn the game as designed. Save the modifications for later waves.
